+`result` is built once, at verification time, and only booleans, integers and
+claim paths are copied out of the disclosed view. `holder_bound` and
+`nonce_bound` are the outcomes of the KB-JWT checks; both are `true` for every
+verified session (a failure is a rejection), and they are stated so a
+consumer does not have to know that. `age_equal_or_over` lists the disclosed
+predicates by bound; it is absent when the wallet disclosed none.
+`credential_exp` is the issuer JWT `exp` (absent when the credential has
+none); an expired credential is rejected, so a verified session's value lies
+in the future at verification time. `disclosed_paths` says WHICH claims the
+wallet revealed, never what they said.
